# API Standards

- Design RESTful endpoints with resource-oriented naming.
- Use correct methods: `GET`, `POST`, `PATCH/PUT`, `DELETE`.
- Keep API status codes accurate (`200`, `201`, `400`, `401`, `403`, `404`, `500`).
- Standardize response shape for success and error cases.
- Enforce authentication and role-based authorization on protected routes.
- Document required params, query, and payload clearly in API docs.
- Ensure list endpoints support pagination, sorting, and filtering.
- Keep API docs in sync whenever endpoint behavior changes.
